map ##NaN :l ##NaN :r)         1 nan=1  collapses\n;;                  (into {} [[##NaN v] [##NaN v]])      collapses (r1 observation)\n;;\n;; Hash collision ruled out: (hash ##NaN) = 2146959360,\n;; (hash (list '+ 'n 0)) = -1050398832. The trigger for the single-session\n;; loss is the seq element itself (also (list 1) loses), not its bucket.\n;;\n;; Conclusion: the whole-element tie IS constructable; retention is\n;; per-constructor (JVM transient/persistent/check paths differ), not a\n;; map-vs-set difference. The r1 \"unconstructable\" claim was a\n;; misdiagnosis: the r1 block's count assertions were calibrated to a\n;; collapsed set, and their failure (3 operands, NaN root seen twice)\n;; actually demonstrated retention with reordering. Reviewer F1 sustained.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-kondo.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-nan-set-probe.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-jvm-order.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-jvm-callsite.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-dart-order.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-node-order.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794932781000-cc4-partial-findings.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-node-callsite.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-node-order.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-dart-order.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-npm.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-jvm-order.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-dart-callsite.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-jolt-order.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-jvm-compiler.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/