\\" \\\"dao/jing\\\" \\\"dao/data\\\" \\\"dao/space\\\" \\\"dao/stream\\\" \\\"yin/vm\\\" \\\"yin/repl\\\"]\\n        bare [\\\"dao/jing_test\\\" \\\"dao/stream_test\\\" \\\"dao/data_test\\\" \\\"yin/vm_test\\\" \\\"yin/repl_test\\\"\\n              \\\"yang/clojure_callsite_test\\\"]\\n        extensions [\\\"clj\\\" \\\"cljc\\\" \\\"cljs\\\" \\\"cljd\\\"]\\n        files (->> (concat\\n                     (mapcat #(->> (fs/glob (fs/path test-root %) \\\"**\\\")\\n                                   (filter (fn [file]\\n                                             (and (fs/regular-file? file)\\n                                                  (re-find #\\\"_test\\\\.(clj|cljc|cljs|cljd)$\\\"\\n                                                           (str file)))))) dirs)\\n                     (for [stem bare ext extensions\\n                           :let [file (fs/path test-root (str stem \\\".\\\" ext))]\\n                           :when (fs/regular-file? file)] file))\\n                   (sort-by str))\",\"numLines\":130,\"startLine\":243,\"totalLines\":786}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"call_cd24d0e785554029bbf876db\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795018441000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.stdout.log:12196:{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1387,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":1,\"session_id\":\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\",\"uuid\":\"f5791997-9c50-45ca-9a09-343d42caf690\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795018441000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.stdout.log:13852:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_20261119002213ad71fd1f23714d3c\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"`assoc` and `conj` are pure VM primitives. `identity`, `inc`, `dec`, `count`, `data/count` — `data/count` comes from the data module (`data/register-data-module`). `identity`/`inc`/`dec` are NOT in vm/primitives. So for runtime tests, use only primitives in the registry: `+ - * / = < > not first rest conj assoc get vec` + data module fns (data/count, data/content=, ...). Or pass an :env with host fns? `compile-and-run` accepts env: `(compile-and-run form {'x 100})` — env maps variables to values. Variables resolve from env — I could bind `inc`? No — variable lookup happens... Let me check how the walker resolves `{:type :variable :name 'inc}` — via env or primitives. If env supplies it, `(compile-and-run '((fn [x] x) 1))`... simpler to use primitives directly: use `(+ x 1)` and `(- x 1)` as dynamic key expressions (both applications, different content). For colliding keys: `{(+ 1 1) :a (+ 2 0) :b}` — both evaluate to 2, different code. Good, and both key exprs are applications of `+`.\\n\\nFor the trace/effect-order tests (family 5): \\\"Record an observable trace using the existing test harness's explicit effects/streams: key-before-value, canonical pair/element order, no duplication, and no later event after an operand failure/continuation transfer.\\\"\\n\\nObservable trace — how do tests record evaluation order? Options: use effectful primitives... `vm/primitives` has no effectful user-callable trace primitive except require/try-require. But `clojure_test` base-vm-opts registers stream module — `(dao.stream.apply/call :op/echo ...)`. Hmm. Alternatively bind host functions in the env: does create-vm's :env supply variable bindings as functions? In `compile-and-run`, env maps var names to values. If I bind `probe` to a host function that appends to an atom, then `(probe 1)` compiles as application of variable `probe` → looks up env → host function → calls it. Does the walker/semantic/stack/register VM support calling host functions from env? The values module presumably wraps host fns. Let me check how env values that are functions get applied — search for tests calling env-supplied functions.\",\"signature\":\"c1eb1a8dcac14dd2bed1e63c\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\",\"uuid\":\"09bd2876-81f8-4e67-affe-ac211a92f4e2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-18T16:22:25.605Z\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":8266,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795018441000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.stdout.log:21236:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_e98ffb13593f4c13beb939fb\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"23:(def ^:private base-vm-opts\\n27:(defn compile-and-run\\n39:(deftest reader-metadata-becomes-occurrence-side-tables\\n55:(deftest indexing-reader-injects-nested-source-positions\\n71:(defn compile-program-and-run\\n83:(deftest test-compile-literals\\n107:(deftest test-set-literal-round-trips\\n114:(deftest test-set-literal-row-lane\\n132:(deftest test-set-in-application-position\\n139:(deftest test-compile-variables\\n145:(deftest test-compile-lambda\\n159:(deftest test-compile-application\\n173:(deftest test-compile-dao-stream-apply-call\\n182:(deftest test-compile-if\\n200:(deftest test-dynamic-collection-literals\\n231:(deftest test-compile-let\\n251:(deftest test-compile-do\\n266:(deftest test-compile-quote\\n272:(deftest test-end-to-end-compilation-and-execution\\n310:(deftest test-compile-errors\\n320:(deftest test-compile-stream-make\\n334:(deftest test-compile-stream-put\\n349:(deftest test-compile-stream-cursor\\n357:(deftest test-compile-stream-next\\n365:(deftest test-stream-end-to-end\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\",\"uuid\":\"848d1dce-6870-4de8-aad0-7933dbf9975f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-18T16:24:52.958Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"23:(def ^:private base-vm-opts\\n27:(defn compile-and-run\\n39:(deftest reader-metadata-becomes-occurrence-side-tables\\n55:(deftest indexing-reader-injects-nested-source-positions\\n71:(defn compile-program-and-run\\n83:(deftest test-compile-literals\\n107:(deftest test-set-literal-round-trips\\n114:(deftest test-set-literal-row-lane\\n132:(deftest test-set-in-application-position\\n139:(deftest test-compile-variables\\n145:(deftest test-compile-lambda\\n159:(deftest test-compile-application\\n173:(deftest test-compile-dao-stream-apply-call\\n182:(deftest test-compile-if\\n200:(deftest test-dynamic-collection-literals\\n231:(deftest test-compile-let\\n251:(deftest test-compile-do\\n266:(deftest test-compile-quote\\n272:(deftest test-end-to-end-compilation-and-execution\\n310:(deftest test-compile-errors\\n320:(deftest test-compile-stream-make\\n334:(deftest test-compile-stream-put\\n349:(deftest test-compile-stream-cursor\\n357:(deftest test-compile-stream-next\\n365:(deftest test-stream-end-to-end\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"call_e98ffb13593f4c13beb939fb\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"subcommandResults\"}}]}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795018441000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.stdout.log:21894:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_202611190025005d62ac797a04411f\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The plain (non-outcome) av lane: `av-opts {:convention :arg-vector :native (set (keys vm/primitives))}` and `av-modules` = default registry + stream + cell + data. Under non-outcome convention, the arity else branch is `(data/count dsg__av)` which the data module refuses with :reason :arity — the payload is the data module's refusal, not the arity-error map. The arity-error map (with :yin.k/fn etc.) only appears with `:outcomes true`. The outcome runner (`run-outcome`) uses outcome-modules = av-modules + 'portable host module with outcome-adapted nth + 'probe. And `outcome-opts {:convention :arg-vector, :outcomes true, :native (set (keys vm/primitives)), :adapters {'data/nth 'portable/nth}}`.\\n\\nWait — but the cohort's unit-opts uses `:adapters library-adapters` and `:native vm/primitive-profiles`. For MY payload-values test I can use a local copy of outcome-opts/outcome-modules (modeled on clojure_test's, portable). Does `run-outcome` work on all hosts? It's in clojure_test.clj (JVM-only) but uses only portable pieces (tu/, yang/outcome-adapter, vm/primitive-profile, module/register-host-module). The callsite test runs on all 4 hosts — does IT use register-host-module anywhere... The r2 report says the callsite battery runs 40 tests on Node/Dart. I'll model my namespace's requires on the callsite test's (which is proven portable on all four hosts): requires clojure.test, dao.jing, yang.clojure, yang.clojure.prelude?, yang.core.call?, yin.vm, yin.vm.encoder, yin.vm.module, yin.vm.data, yin.vm.macro, yin.vm.semantic.linearize, yin.vm.semantic.derive, yin.vm.test-utils?, dao.jing.mem, yin.vm.linker.publish...\\n\\nWait — is `yin.vm.test-utils` portable to Dart/Jolt? It requires dao.stream, dao.stream.memory-log, dao.stream.ringbuffer, dao.stream.observer — cljc files. Are they in the cljd aggregation (bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only)? The Dart lane compiles the namespace + deps. dao.stream.ringbuffer on Dart — dart datagram quirks memory suggests dao.stream works on Dart. The callsite test itself requires `#?@(:clj [[dao.stream :as stream] [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]])` — gated to :clj! So dao.stream IS problematic on non-JVM hosts?? But test-utils requires it ungated... and clojure_test.clj is JVM-only anyway. Hmm — do any PORTABLE (4-host) tests require yin.vm.test-utils? yang.core.call-test — is IT in the J2 included list? No (not listed). Does call_test run on Dart? Let me check cljd_agg to see how namespaces are selected and whether test-utils is Dart-clean.\",\"signature\":\"93169effb67a4e4998a244e0\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\",\"uuid\":\"51f76b76-407e-4792-b3c6-0944d15f3315\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-18T16:25:09.950Z\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":8736,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795018441000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.stdout.log:21896:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_1a726615c62e4d02b3a4c9c4\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"(ns cljd-agg\\n  \\\"Dart test runner that aggregates the generated test files.\\n\\n   `flutter test` loads every generated *_test.dart separately (about 7.5 s\\n   each). This runner compiles the test namespaces through the cljd tool,\\n   groups the generated files into a few shard files that import them and call\\n   each `main`, and runs `flutter test` on the shards only. Shards live under\\n   build/, never under test/, so a plain `cljd test` never runs them twice.\\n\\n   Run with babashka:\\n     bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj [--slow-only | --slow-regex | --only NS,NS...]\\n   --slow-only restricts the run to the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard.\\n   A namespace in that set with no generated Dart file is fatal.\\n   --only compiles and runs only the given test namespaces (bb test:changed,\\n   bb test:sub); one with no generated Dart file is fatal too, EXCEPT a\\n   JVM-only namespace: one whose every deftest sits behind a reader\\n   conditional that excludes ClojureDart (for example\\n   dao.data.sorted-user-type-test). The cljd tool compiles such a namespace as\\n   a plain library (lib/cljd-out/<ns>.dart exists) and emits no test file;\\n   that is reported and skipped, never fatal. A namespace that produced\\n   neither file is still fatal.\\n   --slow-regex prints, for bb.edn, an anchored alternation of those\\n   namespaces with its dots already escaped for embedding in an EDN string\\n   (shadow-cljs --config-merge); it is not a ready-to-use regex. It exits 1\\n   when no namespace uses the guard, so a slow lane cannot be vacuous.\\n   DATOM_SLOW_TESTS is inherited from the environment.\\\"\\n  (:require\\n    [babashka.fs :as fs]\\n    [babashka.process :as p]\\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\\n\\n\\n(def test-root \\\"test\\\")\\n(def out-root \\\"test/cljd-out\\\")\\n(def shard-dir \\\"build/cljd-agg\\\")\\n(def max-shards 8)\\n\\n\\n(defn- ns-of\\n  \\\"The namespace declared by the first ns form of `file`.\\\"\\n  [file]\\n  (second (re-find #\\\"\\\\(ns\\\\s+\\\\^?(?:\\\\{[^}]*\\\\}\\\\s+)?([^\\\\s\\\\)]+)\\\" (slurp file))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- source-files\\n  []\\n  (->> (file-seq (fs/file test-root))\\n       (filter #(re-find #\\\"_test\\\\.clj[cd]$\\\" (str %)))\\n       (remove #(str/includes? (str %) \\\"cljd-out\\\"))\\n       (map str)\\n       sort))\\n\\n\\n(defn- test-namespaces\\n  \\\"Distinct: a namespace with both a .cljc and a .cljd source (for example\\n   dao.stream.cbor-test) has one generated Dart file, which must run once.\\\"\\n  []\\n  (distinct (keep ns-of (source-files))))\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\",\"uuid\":\"76a72f16-b2eb-44b4-b89d-6b84c6ebae69\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-18T16:25:10.182Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"(ns cljd-agg\\n  \\\"Dart test runner that aggregates the generated test files.\\n\\n   `flutter test` loads every generated *_test.dart separately (about 7.5 s\\n   each). This runner compiles the test namespaces through the cljd tool,\\n   groups the generated files into a few shard files that import them and call\\n   each `main`, and runs `flutter test` on the shards only. Shards live under\\n   build/, never under test/, so a plain `cljd test` never runs them twice.\\n\\n   Run with babashka:\\n     bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj [--slow-only | --slow-regex | --only NS,NS...]\\n   --slow-only restricts the run to the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard.\\n   A namespace in that set with no generated Dart file is fatal.\\n   --only compiles and runs only the given test namespaces (bb test:changed,\\n   bb test:sub); one with no generated Dart file is fatal too, EXCEPT a\\n   JVM-only namespace: one whose every deftest sits behind a reader\\n   conditional that excludes ClojureDart (for example\\n   dao.data.sorted-user-type-test). The cljd tool compiles such a namespace as\\n   a plain library (lib/cljd-out/<ns>.dart exists) and emits no test file;\\n   that is reported and skipped, never fatal. A namespace that produced\\n   neither file is still fatal.\\n   --slow-regex prints, for bb.edn, an anchored alternation of those\\n   namespaces with its dots already escaped for embedding in an EDN string\\n   (shadow-cljs --config-merge); it is not a ready-to-use regex. It exits 1\\n   when no namespace uses the guard, so a slow lane cannot be vacuous.\\n   DATOM_SLOW_TESTS is inherited from the environment.\\\"\\n  (:require\\n    [babashka.fs :as fs]\\n    [babashka.process :as p]\\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\\n\\n\\n(def test-root \\\"test\\\")\\n(def out-root \\\"test/cljd-out\\\")\\n(def shard-dir \\\"build/cljd-agg\\\")\\n(def max-shards 8)\\n\\n\\n(defn- ns-of\\n  \\\"The namespace declared by the first ns form of `file`.\\\"\\n  [file]\\n  (second (re-find #\\\"\\\\(ns\\\\s+\\\\^?(?:\\\\{[^}]*\\\\}\\\\s+)?([^\\\\s\\\\)]+)\\\" (slurp file))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- source-files\\n  []\\n  (->> (file-seq (fs/file test-root))\\n       (filter #(re-find #\\\"_test\\\\.clj[cd]$\\\" (str %)))\\n       (remove #(str/includes? (str %) \\\"cljd-out\\\"))\\n       (map str)\\n       sort))\\n\\n\\n(defn- test-namespaces\\n  \\\"Distinct: a namespace with both a .cljc and a .cljd source (for example\\n   dao.stream.cbor-test) has one generated Dart file, which must run once