rry ITS file position — recorded expectation can't hardcode {:line 46...}. So: build the anon no-source form with STRIPPED meta? `(with-meta '(fn [x] x) nil)`? Hmm — reading `'(fn [x] x)` from file gives it meta with file positions. To control: construct `(with-meta (quote (fn [x] x)) nil)`? with-meta nil — meta must be a map or nil — `(with-meta x nil)` works (removes meta? yes, sets meta to nil). But then the INNER forms still carry reader meta — does arity-error-form read `(source-meta form)` of the FN form only — nil meta → no :yin.k/source key → map has 3 pairs [kind, reason, argc]. For the with-source variant use explicit {:line 7 :column 2}. Recorded expectations: for the nil-meta variant, key order [:yin.k/kind :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc] (roots: kind 476c5dac, reason 81b62c1e, argc 8930bf5e → sorted [47, 81, 89] = kind, reason, argc ✓).\\n\\nNow — WAIT, one more critical check. The arity-error-form builds the map via `cond->`/`assoc` — a HOST map built at COMPILE time. Its iteration order (host) feeds the emitter. With my fix, the emitter sorts — deterministic. But there's a subtlety: `cond->` assoc order builds an array-map on JVM with ≤8 entries: {:yin.vm.data/reason :arity, :yin.k/argc ..., :yin.k/fn ..., :yin.k/kind ..., :yin.k/source ...} — insertion order fixed. Post-fix irrelevant. ✓\\n\\nAnother subtlety — `compile-av-fn` may build maps with MORE structure — fine.\\n\\nNow the LEGACY fixture capture. Also the RECORDING of digests. Order of work (TDD):\\n\\n1. Write capture namespace for the legacy pre-fix fixture (runs NOW at pre-fix compiler) → writes CBOR + prints old root/value. **Must run BEFORE implementing the fix.**\\n2. Write the full test namespace with all expectations except the post-fix recorded digests (family 1d/recorded child-address vector — those are fix-invariant! I already HAVE them from the diagnostics: the operand-root vector post-fix = [201f235c, 1e03667e, 3156a070, 81b62c1e, 1db5dbd0, 8930bf5e, e60543d2] — recorded NOW, v