e, and the manifest/legacy boundaries of the c1-2 revision.\\n\\n   The oracle builders here are independent of the emitter's helper: children\\n   project through yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode and order through\\n   dao.jing/canonical-compare, never through the sort the emitter performs.\\\")\\n```\\n\\nrequires: clojure.test, clojure.walk, dao.jing, dao.jing.cbor, dao.stream.base64, yang.clojure, yang.core.uast, yin.vm, yin.vm.ast-walker, yin.vm.data, yin.vm.encoder, yin.vm.macro, yin.vm.module, yin.vm.semantic, yin.vm.semantic.derive, yin.vm.semantic.linearize, yin.vm.debruijn.stack, yin.vm.debruijn.register, yin.vm.test-utils.\\n\\nPortability of yin.vm.debruijn.stack/register on jolt: they're in the J2 included list via their tests (yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test etc.) ✓.\\n\\nSections:\\n\\n**§0 helpers** (as planned).\\n\\n**§1 Family 1 — arity-map regression:**\\n\\n```clojure\\n(def ^:private cohort-forms\\n  \\\"The cc4 cohort's argument-vector/lower-unit source (r2 evidence): the\\n   named-arity constructor is the reproduced divergence.\\\"\\n  '[(defn replay [x] (let [[a b] [x 1.5]] (+ (identity ^:replay a) (identity ^:replay a) b)))\\n    (replay 2)])\\n```\\nWait — the cohort source is multi-line; same forms. ✓\\n\\n```clojure\\n(def ^:private arity-map-key-order\\n  \\\"The ruled pair order of the named arity map: key roots 1e0366… (:yin.k/fn),\\n   81b62c… (:yin.vm.data/reason), 8930bf… (:yin.k/argc) — pinned by the ruling\\n   from the unchanged child rows of both hosts' pre-fix evidence.\\\"\\n  [:yin.k/fn :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc])\\n\\n(def ^:private named-arity-operand-roots\\n  \\\"Recorded on the JVM; the child addresses are compiler-revision-stable\\n   content addresses (each child compiled identically before and after the\\n   ordering fix).\\\"\\n  [:segment/blake3-201f235c…  seed {}\\n   :segment/blake3-1e03667e…  :yin.k/fn\\n   :segment/blake3-3156a070…  'replay\\n   :segment/blake3-81b62c1e…  :yin.vm.data/reason\\n   :segment/blake3-1db5dbd0…  :arity\\n   :segment/blake3-8930bf5e…  :yin.k/argc\\n   :segment/blake3-e60543d2…]) ; (data/count dsg__av)\\n```\\n\\nFinder for arity constructors:\\n\\n```clojure\\n(defn- arity-map-constructors\\n  \\\"The constructed maps naming an arity error: key :yin.k/fn (named) or\\n   :yin.k/kind (anonymous) among the operand literals.\\\"\\n  [ast]\\n  (into [] (filter (fn [c] (some (fn [o] (and (= :literal (:type o))\\n                                              (contains? #{:yin.k/fn :yin.k/kind} (:value o))))\\n                                 (:operands c))))\\n        (collection-applications ast)))\\n```\\n\\ndeftest `arity-map-canonical-order-test`:\\n- for BOTH `(yang/compile-program cohort-forms true yang/unit-opts)` and `(yang/lower-unit cohort-forms)`:\\n  - constructors exist; named ones (:yin.k/fn) — for lower-unit there are TWO (replay + identity from library); assert for each:\\n    - key-literal vector = [:yin.k/fn :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc]\\n    - operand-roots = named-arity-operand-roots\\n    - pair-keys sorted (oracle)\\n    - seed first, even operand count\\n    - the argc value is a (data/count dsg__av) application; fn value literal 'replay or 'identity\\n- anonymous: compile `[(with-meta '(fn [x] x) nil)]` and `[(with-meta '(fn [x] x) {:line 7 :column 2})]` under unit-opts:\\n  - key order [:yin.k/kind :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc] (nil-meta: 3 pairs)\\n  - with-source: [:yin.k/kind :yin.k/source :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc], :yin.k/source value {:line 7 :column 2}\\n  - operand roots recorded vectors for both\\n- payload values at runtime (outcome lane): local outcome-opts/modules; run `[(defn arity2 [x] x) (arity2 1 2)]` → [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/fn 'arity2 :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/argc 2}] — value = map equality (order-free). Also anonymous → {:yin.k/kind :anonymous :yin.k/argc 1 ...}.\\n\\nHmm wait — with :outcomes, `defn arity2` compiles to av-fn; call with 2 args → argc=2. The error payload — let me confirm the runtime shape by trying. I'll write it and adjust after running.\\n\\n**§2 Family 2 — map permutations.**\\n\\nCorpus definition. Represent each case as `[label entries]` where entries is a vector of `[key-form value-form]`.\\n\\n```clojure\\n(def ^:private map-corpus\\n  \\\"Recorded corpus (ruling test 2): distinct source-entry pairs. Every case\\n   holds at least one dynamic expression.\\\"\\n  [[:constant-keys-dynamic-values [[:a '(+ n 0)] [:b '(+ n 1)]]]\\n   [:dynamic-keys [['(first xs) :v1] ['(first (rest xs)) :v2]]]\\n   [:heterogeneous-scalar-keys\\n    [[:kw '(+ n 0)] [\\\"str\\\" 1] [3 1.5] ['sym '(rest xs)] [(quote true) 0] [nil 2]]]\\n```\\nHmm wait — entry `[nil 2]`: constant; `[\\\"str\\\" 1]` constant... the MAP needs ≥1 dynamic to reach the emitter — `:kw '(+ n 0)` provides it. Heterogeneous keys: keyword, string, long, double, symbol, boolean, nil, quoted collection, quoted collection with metadata. Values mostly constants.\\n\\nQuoted collection key: `'(quote [1 2])`; with-meta: build form at runtime: `(list 'quote (with-meta '[1 2] {:sem true}))`. Corpus entries built as DATA at load time — fine (deterministic).\\n\\n   [:nested-collections\\n    [[:map '{:inner (+ n 1)}] [:set '#{(+ n 2) 3}] [:vec '[(+ n 3)]] [:deep '{:a #{[(+ n 4)]}}]]]\\n   [:floats [[1.5 '(+ n 1.5)] [2.25 -0.5] ['##Inf? no...]]]  — careful: ##Inf readable? skip Inf. floats: 1.5, -0.5, 2.25e-3?\\n   [:duplicate-subtrees [[:a '(first xs)] [:b '(first xs)] [:c '(first xs)]]]\\n   [:meta-carrying-keys [(quoted-with-meta...) ...]]])\\n```\\n\\nWait — `'#{(+ n 2) 3}` inside a quoted form? I'm writing entries as quoted data in the test file — `'[:map '{:inner (+ n 1)}]` — the inner quote gives the FORM {:inner (+ n 1)} ✓ (a map with dynamic content used as a value → constructed recursively).\\n\\nSizes corpus: generated:\\n```clojure\\n(defn- sized-entries [n] (into [] (map (fn [i] [(keyword (str \\\"k\\\" i)) (list '+ 'n i)])) (range n)))\\n```\\nSizes 8 9 16 32 → also a dynamic-key variant `[(list '+ 'n i) (keyword ...)]`?\\n\\nPermutations:\\n```clojure\\n(defn- all-permutations [n] ...) ;; 0..4\\n(defn- recorded-permutations [n seed] ;; forward, reverse, rotations 1 2 3, lcg shuffle\\n  ...)\\n```\\n\\nRepresentations:\\n```clojure\\n(defn- map-representations\\n  \\\"The same logical entries as host values: insertion-ordered array-maps,\\n   hash-maps, and (small sizes) a file-literal array map.\\\"\\n  [entries]\\n  (let [flat (mapcat identity entries)]\\n    (into []\\n          (comp\\n            (distinct?? no)\\n          [(apply array-map flat)\\n           (apply hash-map flat)])))\\n```\\nHmm — `distinct` not needed. For permutation p: `(apply array-map (permute flat p))`.\\n\\nSnapshot & compare:\\n```clojure\\n(deftest map-permutation-invariance-test\\n  (doseq [[label entries] (cons ... map-corpus, sized cases)]\\n    (testing (str label)\\n      (let [variants (for [perm (perms (count entries))\\n                           :let [pe (permute-entries entries perm)]\\n                           rep [array-map-fn hash-map-fn]\\n                           :let [form (build rep pe)]]\\n                       form)\\n            snaps (mapv #(snapshot-of (yang/compile %)) variants)]\\n        (is (apply = snaps) ...)\\n        (doseq [ast ...] (is (ctor-pairs-sorted? ast)))))))\\n```\\n\\nsnapshot-of: compile → encoder/project → tree+rows → digests (root, keys, c1, provenance). \\n\\nPermutation count control: sizes 0-4 all perms; 8/9/16/32 recorded set (forward, reverse, rot1..3, shuffle ×2 seeds) × 2 reps. Map building cost: compile 32-entry map with permutations — each compile projects 64 children... fine.\\n\\n**§3 Family 3 — sets.** Mirror with set corpus:\\n```clojure\\n[:dynamic-elements ['(+ n 0) '(first xs) ...]]\\n[:nested-dynamic-sets ['#{(+ n 1)} '(second xs) 2]]\\n[:colliding-value-expressions ['(mod n 2)?? — no mod primitive needed for COMPILE-only] ...]\\n```\\n\\\"Include nested dynamic sets and different expressions evaluating to the same value\\\" — compile-time: two different exprs `(first xs)` and `'(first xs)`... same-value needs runtime — execution covers it; corpus includes the forms. Representations: `(set (vec elems-in-perm-order))` — hmm `(set v)` dedups by value — the ELEMENTS are FORMS (distinct lists), so set keeps all. Also `apply hash-set`. For array-set? No array-set in clojure — sorted-set? \\\"available ordinary\\\" representations — literal #{} from file, `(set ...)`, `(apply hash-set ...)`. On hosts, `hash-set` iteration differs (JVM hash vs Dart hash) → post-fix invariant anyway.\\n\\nElement sort key: single root. Assert sortedness oracle + snapshot invariance across permutations/representations.\\n\\n**§4 Family 4 — oracle:**\\n```clojure\\n(deftest order-pairing-multiplicity-oracle-test ...)\\n```\\n- for each corpus map compile: seed-first, even count, pair-keys sorted, pairs match independently compiled entries (multiset), metadata invariance (with-meta variants), tie preservation (identical pairs kept: `{x :v x :v}` — construct with duplicate keys? A HOST MAP CANNOT HAVE DUPLICATE KEYS — `{x :v x :v}` evaluates to {x :v} — one entry! Duplicate ENTRIES can't exist in a host map. Hmm! \\\"add distinct forms compiling to an identical entire pair/element to exercise ties without occurrence loss\\\" — for MAPS: distinct forms that compile to the same PAIR — e.g. key `(quote x)` vs `x`? compile differently. Key `x` value `(+ n 0)` vs key `x` value... identical pair means identical key code AND value code: two DIFFERENT source forms compiling to identical code: e.g. key `x` (symbol) vs key form `(quote x)`? no that's quoted data. How about values: `(+ n 0)` and... two syntactically different forms with same compile: `(+ n 0)` vs `(+ n 0)` with different metadata! `(with-meta '(+ n 0) {:line 5})` vs plain — same projected content (meta dropped), different source. That's the tie: two entries whose compiled pairs are content-identical → equal sort keys → both occurrences preserved (4 operands for 2 entries). For SETS: `#{(+ n 0) (+ n 0)}` — host set DEDUPES identical forms by value! Two IDENTICAL forms are = → one element. So ties in sets need distinct-but-equivalent forms: `#{(with-meta '(+ n 0) {:line 9}) (+ n 0)}` — distinct host values (different meta) → set keeps 2 → both compile to identical code → tie. ✓ Same trick for maps.\\n\\n- \\\"Changing only source-position or variable-node metadata MUST NOT change code order/root\\\": compile plain vs with-meta-positions → same root; and the operand-root vectors equal.\\n- \\\"Preserve semantic metadata in literal payloads\\\": quoted-with-meta key vs without → roots DIFFER (metadata is content) — both orders still sorted.\\n\\n**§5 Family 5 — execution** (as planned).\\n\\n**§6 Family 6 — entry points + macro.**\\n\\n**§7 Family 7 — legacy + tokens.**\\n\\nAlso needed: `expand-like-the-repl` local copy (macro seed/expand) — requires yin.vm.macro ✓.\\n\\nLength concern: this namespace will be ~600-800 lines. That's expected for this codebase's test style.\\n\\nOne more mechanical detail — `vm/ast->semantic-bytecode` returns `{:root ...}` where root is a keyword `:segment/blake3-…`. `jing/canonical-compare` over VECTORS of these keywords ✓.\\n\\nNow about `(sort jing/canonical-compare coll)` — sorting EDN tuples containing keywords/vectors ✓ (cohort does this).\\n\\nWriting now. I'll be careful with quote levels. Also remember: cljd lane — avoid `(quote ...)` inside #{} reader? Sets as data fine. Avoid regex, avoid `->>` with lazy? fine.\\n\\nOne CLJS gotcha: `(apply array-map flat)` where flat is seq — OK. `(apply hash-map flat)` OK. On cljd — array-map/hash-map exist ✓.\\n\\nDart: `keyword` fn `(keyword (str \\\"k\\\" i))` ✓.\\n\\nAnother gotcha: on CLJS, `=` of my snapshot maps with keyword keys ✓.\\n\\nLet me also decide the snapshot to include `:applications` count (cohort has it) — count of marked occurrences — permutation-invariant post-fix ✓.\\n\\nFor the stack/register image opts — cohort used `{:segment-address :cc4/stack :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)}` — mirror with :fixorder/stack.\\n\\n`linearize/project-rows tree nil rows` — signature (tree, ?, rows) with nil for what? In cohort: `(linearize/project-rows tree nil rows)`. Check signature quickly.\",\"signature\":\"33b0b6f675cd4fff8b3175a3\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\",\"uuid\":\"6ddd8e9c-e17a-4869-8b3e-6766d0b5a374\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-18T16:38:24.983Z\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":55232,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795018441000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.stdout.log:46082:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_20261119003831680aa2b1025246a7\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_730840fc1b9e4241b395d4ea\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nsrc = r'''(ns yang.clojure-collection-order-test\\n  \\\"Constructed collections v1 (architect ruling 1795017757000, RULING 1-4):\\n   the canonical operand ordering of dynamically constructed map and set\\n   literals at yang.clojure's collection emitter, the evaluation semantics\\n   that ordering makes executable, and the manifest/legacy boundaries of the\\n   c1-2 revision.\\n\\n   Every order expectation here comes from builders independent of the\\n   emitter's own sort: children project through\\n   yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode and order through dao.jing/canonical-compare\\n   (RFC 8949 canonical bytes, unsigned bytewise, proper prefix first), the\\n   same comparator the ruling names — never through the helper under test.\\\"\\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\n            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]\\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\\n            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Independent oracle builders (RULING 1's comparator, not the emitter's sort)\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(defn- collection-applications\\n  \\\"Every constructor application of compiled `ast` — an assoc over the {}\\n   seed or a conj over the []/#{} seed — outermost walk order. A program\\n   under test contains either only emitter output or only the explicit\\n   constructor calls a control names, never both.\\\"\\n  [ast]\\n  (let [acc (atom [])]\\n    (walk/postwalk\\n      (fn [n]\\n        (when (and (map? n)\\n                   (= :application (:type n))\\n                   (= :variable (get-in n [:operator :type]))\\n                   (= :literal (get-in n [:operands 0 :type]))\\n                   (contains? #{['assoc {}] ['conj []] ['conj #{}]}\\n                              [(get-in n [:operator :name])\\n                               (get-in n [:operands 0 :value])]))\\n          (swap! acc conj n))\\n        n)\\n      ast)\\n    @acc))\\n\\n(defn- map-constructors [ast]\\n  (into [] (filter #(= (quote assoc) (get-in % [:operator :name])))\\n        (collection-applications ast)))\\n\\n(defn- child-roots\\n  \\\"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of each operand of `node`,\\n   projected independently of the emitter.\\\"\\n  [node]\\n  (mapv (fn [o] (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode o))) (:operands node)))\\n\\n(defn- seed-root\\n  \\\"The recorded root of the empty-map seed literal (a content address:\\n   stable across hosts and compiler revisions).\\\"\\n  []\\n  :segment/blake3-201f235cbac998f43954454e9df0eb633717e79de535776f3f51e198a3759b10)\\n\\n(defn- pair-keys\\n  \\\"The RULING 1 sort keys of a map constructor's pairs: `[key-root\\n   value-root]` per source pair, in emitted order.\\\"\\n  [node]\\n  (mapv vec (partition 2 (rest (child-roots node)))))\\n\\n(defn- element-keys\\n  \\\"The RULING 1 sort keys of a set constructor's elements (one root each),\\n   in emitted order.\\\"\\n  [node]\\n  (mapv vector (rest (child-roots node))))\\n\\n(defn- ascending?\\n  \\\"True when `ks` is strictly sorted by jing/canonical-compare; equal keys\\n   are equal executable content and a tie is legal anywhere.\\\"\\n  [ks]\\n  (every? (fn [[a b]] (neg? (jing/canonical-compare a b)))\\n          (partition 2 1 ks)))\\n\\n(defn- key-literals\\n  \\\"Every second operand's literal value (the map keys), for reading an\\n   emitted order against recorded expectations.\\\"\\n  [node]\\n  (mapv (fn [o] (when (= :literal (:type o)) (:value o)))\\n        (take-nth 2 (rest (:operands node)))))\\n\\n(defn- project-batch\\n  \\\"One compiled ast through the production encoder envelope under `token`.\\\"\\n  ([ast] (project-batch ast \\\"order-a\\\"))\\n  ([ast token]\\n   (let [p (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\\n     {:tree (first (:yin/batch p))\\n      :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)})))\\n\\n(defn- digest-snapshot\\n  \\\"The equality snapshot of one projected batch: root, the canonical-sorted\\n   C1 marker relation, the sorted occurrence-key vector and all three\\n   instruction formats' call-provenance — the cohort's model, nothing\\n   normalized away.\\\"\\n  [{:keys [tree rows]}]\\n  (let [c1 (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\\n                      (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) rows)))\\n        keys (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\\n                        (into [] (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\\n                                       (map #(vec (take 3 %)))) rows)))\\n        sem (linearize/project-rows tree nil rows)\\n        stack (derive/stack-image (:vector sem)\\n                                  {:segment-address :order/stack\\n                                   :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})\\n        register (derive/register-image (:vector sem)\\n                                        {:segment-address :order/register\\n                                         :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})]\\n    {:root (:root tree)\\n     :applications (count keys)\\n     :keys-digest (jing/content-hash keys)\\n     :c1-digest (jing/content-hash c1)\\n     :instruction-provenance-digest\\n     (jing/content-hash [(:call-provenance sem)\\n                         (:call-provenance stack)\\n                         (:call-provenance register)])}))\\n\\n(defn- compile-snapshot\\n  \\\"Compile `form`, project it, digest it.\\\"\\n  [form]\\n  (digest-snapshot (project-batch (yang/compile form))))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Execution routes (RULING 2/3: walker, semantic, stack, register)\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(def ^:private registry\\n  (-> (module/empty-registry)\\n      module/register-cell-module\\n      data/register-data-module))\\n\\n(def ^:private base-opts\\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\\n   :capability-secret tu/secret\\n   :primitives vm/primitives\\n   :modules registry})\\n\\n(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\\n\\n(defn- run-on\\n  \\\"Run compiled `ast` on every execution route, returning lane -> value.\\\"\\n  ([ast] (run-on ast {}))\\n  ([ast env]\\n   (let [opts (assoc base-opts :env env)\\n         runners\\n         {:ast-walker (fn [] (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast))\\n          :semantic (fn [] (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\\n                                                      (vm/ast->datoms ast))))\\n          :stack (fn [] (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\\n                                  (:image (derive/stack-image\\n                                            (:vector (linearize/project ast))))\\n                                  (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))))\\n          :register (fn [] (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\\n                                     (derive/register-image\\n                                       (:vector (linearize/project ast)))\\n                                     (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))}]\\n     (into {} (map (fn [[lane run]] [lane (vm/value (run))])) runners))))\\n\\n(defn- run-form\\n  \\\"Compile and run `form` on every route with `env`.\\\"\\n  ([form] (run-form form {}))\\n  ([form env] (run-on (yang/compile form) env)))\\n\\n(defn- trace-of\\n  \\\"The observable trace of `form` on every route: each lane's value and the\\n   ordered log the env-bound `tap` host function recorded while producing\\n   it. `tap` echoes its argument, so the log is the operand evaluation\\n   order.\\\"\\n  ([form] (trace-of form {}))\\n  ([form env]\\n   (let [log (atom [])]\\n     (into {}\\n           (map (fn [[lane value]] [lane {:value value :log @log}]))\\n           (do (reset! log [])\\n               (run-form form (assoc env 'tap (fn [x] (swap! log conj x) x))))))))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Deterministic permutation machinery (RULING 3: recorded data, no host rand)\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(defn- all-permutations\\n  \\\"Every ordering of (range n), the plain recursive enumeration.\\\"\\n  [n]\\n  (if (zero? n)\\n    [[]]\\n    (mapcat (fn [i]\\n              (map #(into [i] %)\\n                   (all-permutations (remove #{i} (range n)))))\\n            (range n))))\\n\\n(defn- rotate\\n  \\\"The kth rotation of `v`.\\\"\\n  [k v]\\n  (let [k (mod k (count v))]\\n    (into (subvec v k) (subvec v 0 k))))\\n\\n(defn- lcg\\n  \\\"The recorded-seed Lehmer generator: x' = 48271*x mod (2^31-2). Every\\n   product stays below 2^53, so every host's double arithmetic computes the\\n   identical sequence (a JVM long-math generator would not be portable).\\\"\\n  [seed n]\\n  (into [] (map (fn [_ x] (mod (* 48271 x) 2147483646)) (repeat n 0))\\n        (rest (iterate (fn [x] (mod (* 48271 x) 2147483646)) seed))))\\n\\n(defn- lcg-shuffle\\n  \\\"Fisher-Yates over `v` driven by the recorded-seed Lehmer generator.\\\"\\n  [seed v]\\n  (let [n (count v)]\\n    (if (< n 2)\\n      (vec v)\\n      (let [states (lcg seed (dec n))]\\n        (loop [i (dec n), s states, acc (vec v)]\\n          (if (zero? i)\\n            acc\\n            (let [j (mod (first s) (inc i))]\\n              (recur (dec i) (rest s)\\n                     (assoc acc i (nth acc j) j (nth acc i))))))))))\\n\\n(defn- recorded-permutations\\n  \\\"The recorded permutation set for sizes beyond the full enumeration:\\n   forward, reverse, four rotations and two seeded shuffles.\\\"\\n  [n seed]\\n  (into []\\n        (map vec)\\n        [(range n)\\n         (reverse (range n))\\n         (rotate 1 (vec (range n)))\\n         (rotate 2 (vec (range n)))\\n         (rotate 3 (vec (range n)))\\n         (lcg-shuffle seed (vec (range n)))\\n         (lcg-shuffle (inc seed) (vec (range n)))]))\\n\\n(defn- permute\\n  \\\"The entries of `v` reordered by index vector `p`.\\\"\\n  [v p]\\n  (into [] (map v) p))\\n\\n(defn- build-map\\n  \\\"The logical entries as a host map value in `order`, through the array-map\\n   or hash-map representation.\\\"\\n  [rep entries]\\n  (let [flat (into [] (mapcat identity) entries)]\\n    (if (= :array-map rep)\\n      (apply array-map flat)\\n      (apply hash-map flat))))\\n'''\\nPath(\\\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\\\").write_text(src)\\nprint(\\\"part1 written\\\", len(src))\\nPYEOF\",\"description\":\"Write test namespace part 1 (helpers)\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\",\"uuid\":\"1e1c5d85-861b-47a7-9f28-18c211a6a264\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-18T16:39:06.273Z\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"call_730840fc1b9e4241b395d4ea\":{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nsrc = r'''(ns yang.clojure-collection-order-test\\n  \\\"Constructed collections v1 (architect ruling 1795017757000, RULING 1-4):\\n   the canonical operand ordering of dynamically constructed map and set\\n   literals at yang.clojure's collection emitter, the evaluation semantics\\n   that ordering makes executable, and the manifest/legacy boundaries of the\\n   c1-2 revision.\\n\\n   Every order expectation here comes from builders independent of the\\n   emitter's own sort: children project through\\n   yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode and order through dao.jing/canonical-compare\\n   (RFC 8949 canonical bytes, unsigned bytewise, proper prefix first), the\\n   same comparator the ruling names — never through the helper under test.\\\"\\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\n            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]\\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\\n            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\\n            [