ay-map; its ordinary map is the\\n  recorded substitute — the test documents this), set-over-vector and\\n  hash-set.\\n- **Family 4**: the whole-element/whole-pair tie needed two host-unequal\\n  forms compiling to one content. **NaN keys** are the only such pair for\\n  maps (never `=`, one quiet-NaN row) and reach both the value-root\\n  secondary key and the identical-pair tie; the tests build them with\\n  `assoc`/`into` because map/set literals reject or collapse NaN\\n  duplicates under Java `equals`. **A whole-element tie for sets is\\n  unconstructable at the form boundary** (every available host set\\n  constructor collapses two NaNs); this is recorded in the test as a\\n  boundary, not skipped silently — occurrence preservation is asserted\\n  with ordinary distinct elements. Also: two metadata-variants of one\\n  value cannot coexist as map keys (host `=` ignores metadata, so the host\\n  map collapses them silently) — the corpus uses distinct values and\\n  metadata-as-content is asserted across separate compilations.\\n- **Family 5**: all four routes (walker, semantic, stack, register) run\\n  each fixture; traces come from an env-bound host `tap` that echoes its\\n  argument. Colliding dynamic keys: the canonically last pair wins on\\n  every route, and both insertion orders agree. The failure/transfer case\\n  asserts the trace stops before later operands and at least one route\\n  surfaces the raise. Explicit `assoc`/`conj`, dynamic vectors, `let` and\\n  `do` keep written order, their swaps stay observable, and the swapped\\n  orders remain distinct canonical code (the invalid-global-sorter\\n  controls).\\n- **Family 6**: `compile-form`, `compile`, both `compile-program` modes and\\n  `lower-unit` emit one operand vector (native trio exactly equal; the\\n  convention entries compile free names through adapters, so they are\\n  compared with each other and by the comparator, as before the fix); the\\n  production twin-call macro fixture expands with `:ok` status, unfabricated\\n  origins and the constructed map intact.\\n- **Family 7**: the c1-1 legacy row set loads through\\n  `ast-walker/vm-load-rows` and executes WITHOUT recompilation to its old\\n  value `{0 :b}` while the same source freshly compiled under c1-2 yields\\n  `{0 :a}` (the canonical order changes which colliding pair is last) —\\n  old artifacts keep old executable behavior. The unannotated\\n  legacy-load/missing-C1 refusal tests remain in the callsite battery\\n  (untouched, green). Two admission tokens: one root, different origins\\n  and key vectors (cohort negative member + the new namespace's copy).\\n- **Dart compile note**: the first Dart ordering run failed to compile —\\n  ClojureDart has no `array-map`; fixed with the `insertion-map` builder\\n  (reader-conditional), documented in the test. JVM/Node re-verified green\\n  after that change.\\n\\n## Dependencies outside the bounds table (reported, not fixed)\\n\\n1. **J2's inherited manifest refusal** (the four unlisted namespaces) — the\\n   Jolt owner must reconcile them before Jolt can execute either battery.\\n   This round's Jolt gates are recorded as refused, not green.\\n2. None other: no Jing/CBOR, VM grammar/evaluator, macro.cljc, semantic\\n   lowering, encoder/loader, core prelude, dht.cljc or slice9 tables were\\n   touched; hashing, C1 validation, origins and the oracle are unchanged.\\n\\n## cc4 adoption status (unchanged by this round)\\n\\nThe fix closes the compiler-determinism defect; cc4's declared B/S,\\npre/post-port and cross-check-host budget work remains for a separately\\nauthorized round, per the ruling. D1 stays dissolved. This ordering fix is\\npinned separately from Phase 2 `d60038ef`.\\n\\n## SHA-256 pins at delivery (pre-commit)\\n\\n| File | SHA-256 |\\n|---|---|\\n| `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` | `{SHA_CLOJURE}` |\\n| `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` | `{SHA_FRONTENDS}` |\\n| `test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc` | `{SHA_ORDER}` |\\n| `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` | `{SHA_CALLSITE}` |\\n| `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` | `{SHA_J2}` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots.edn` | `{SHA_SNAP}` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots-prefix-c1-1.edn` | `{SHA_SNAP_PRE}` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/constructed-collections-legacy-c1-1.cbor` | `{SHA_LEGACY}` |\\n\\nThe temporary driver namespace (`test/fixorder_tmp_gen_test.cljc`) and the\\ntwo scratch namespaces are deleted at delivery; the exact commands above\\nplus their logs are retained in\\n`collab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/`.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\ndoc = doc.replace(\\\"{Q}\\\", Q)\\nPath(\\\"collab/yang-clojure/1795028788000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.findings.md.partial\\\").write_text(doc)\\nprint(\\\"skeleton written\\\")\\nPYEOF\",\"description\":\"Write findings document skeleton\"}}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795018441000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.stdout.log:99624:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_20261119031340da726e24fb44411c\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_cd967665d81f41008cd27777\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\ndoc = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n## Test-family notes and boundaries (reported, not worked around)\\n\\n- Family 1: named (replay + the library's identity) and anonymous arity\\n  maps (with and without reader source metadata) asserted by key-literal\\n  order, recorded child-address vector, sortedness oracle, and runtime\\n  payload values on the outcome lane ([:yin.k/error ...] maps verified).\\n  Whole-tree/root/C1/provenance equality for the two members is the\\n  re-pinned cohort (same source, options, coordinates), now matching on\\n  JVM/Node/Dart.\\n- Family 2/3: sizes 0-4 fully enumerated; 8/9/16/32 with forward, reverse,\\n  four rotations and two seeded Lehmer shuffles